🧾 General Tasks
-Check emails and respond to project-related messages
-Update task manager (Trello, Asana, Notion, etc.)
-Attend team/client meetings or stand-ups
-Track project time and submit timesheets (if needed)
-Backup or version-control design files
-Review feedback from previous sessions
-Stay updated on web design tools and trends
-Document design decisions for future reference
-Collaborate with developers, copywriters, or marketers
-Optimize workflow and file performance (e.g., reduce file size, organize assets)
-Join the teams discord https://discord.gg/CJ5cYUJUYr

🧩 Project Preparation
-Gather client/project requirements (brief, branding guidelines, user personas)
-Create or review project scope and milestones
-Research competitors and industry design trends
-Create a mood board or style guide
-Select typefaces, color palette, and visual language

🎨 Design File Setup
-Create artboards or frames for key screen sizes (desktop, tablet, mobile)
-Set up a design system (component, symbols, styles)
-Organize layers and naming conventions
-Define grid systems and layout constraints
-Set up reusable UI components (buttons, inputs, navs)

📱 UI/UX Design Tasks
-Design wireframes for each key page/screen
-Create high-fidelity mockups
-Ensure responsive design for all breakpoints
-Prototype user flows (navigation, modals, etc.)
-Add interactions and animations (if applicable)

✅ Review & Feedback
-Perform internal QA of design file (spacing, alignments, fonts)
-Share DF with client/team for feedback
-Implement feedback and iterate
-Prepare for developer handoff

🛠️ Developer Handoff
-Annotate components and specs
-Export assets (SVGs, PNGs, WebP, etc.)
-Link the DF in tools like Zeplin, Figma Inspect, or Storybook
-Provide a style guide or documentation
-Confirm accessibility considerations (color contrast, alt text, etc.)
